Ask before chrome://password-manager shows, copies, edits or exports a
password on OHOS.

PasswordsPrivateDelegateImpl::AuthenticateUser asks only on Mac, Windows and
ChromeOS and runs the callback with true everywhere else, so on a tablet or a
PC the native password page handed out every password without asking. On
OHOS it now asks with HarmonyOS's own prompt -- the authenticator filling
already uses (ohos-password-reauth.patch) -- with the validity the page asks
for: a minute to view, none to export. Without an authenticator, because the
shell is not attached, the answer is no; with nothing enrolled on the device
the authenticator says no itself and tells the shell, which can ask the user
to set a lock screen.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

